# VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client requests for the local stack (tilt up).

@agent = http://localhost:8080
@app = http://localhost:8081
@sessionId = local-session-000000000000000000000001

### Agent health
GET {{agent}}/ping

### Invoke the agent directly (bypasses Slack)
POST {{agent}}/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: {{sessionId}}

{
  "prompt": "What is my LinkedIn name?",
  "userId": "slack-TLOCALDEV1-ULOCALDEV1",
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
}

### Local gateway health
GET {{app}}/healthz

### Our CIMD client metadata document -- this URL is our OAuth client_id.
### `client_id` in the response must equal the URL it was fetched from.
GET {{app}}/oauth2/client-metadata.json

### Ask a CIMD provider something (needs CIMD_TOKEN_TABLE + a public PUBLIC_BASE_URL)
POST {{agent}}/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: {{sessionId}}

{
  "prompt": "What are my open Linear issues?",
  "userId": "slack-TLOCALDEV1-ULOCALDEV1",
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
}

### Read a public link (fetch_url)
POST {{agent}}/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: {{sessionId}}

{
  "prompt": "Summarise https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.13.html in 3 bullets",
  "userId": "slack-TLOCALDEV1-ULOCALDEV1",
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
}

### A message that is only a file. Replace the ID with a real Slack file ID (F...) and
### set SLACK_BOT_TOKEN (with files:read) for the agent to download it.
POST {{agent}}/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: {{sessionId}}

{
  "prompt": "",
  "files": [{"id": "F0123ABCDEF", "name": "invoice-sept.pdf", "mimetype": "application/pdf", "size": 52000}],
  "userId": "slack-TLOCALDEV1-ULOCALDEV1",
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
}

### Slack events need a valid signature: use scripts/send_test_event.py instead.
